# Packaging filter for `vsce package --no-dependencies` / `vsce ls`.
#
# The VSIX carries only the runtime artefact: the manifest, the changelog, the
# license, the icons and the bundles under dist/. Everything else (src/**,
# test/**, node_modules/**, tsconfig*.json, esbuild.mjs, vite.config.ts,
# .vscode-test*, .tsbuild/**, .env*, *.sqlite*, logs) is excluded by the first
# rule and never re-included.
#
# vsce does NOT apply these rules in order: a file ships when it matches no
# exclusion OR matches any `!` rule. A later exclusion cannot cut a path back
# out of a broader `!` rule, so dist/ is re-included subtree by subtree (the
# names are the layout contract of esbuild.mjs and vite.config.ts), and
# dist/test/** (the compiled extension-host suites) is simply never listed.

# exclude everything
**

# ship only the runtime artefact
!package.json
!CHANGELOG.md
# generated copy of the repository-root LICENSE, staged by `esbuild.mjs --package`;
# vsce warns and asks whether to continue when no license is packaged
!LICENSE
!media/**
# extension host bundle, main in package.json
!dist/extension.js
!dist/extension.js.map
# embedded coordination service: bundle, ESM marker, prompts, store DDL
!dist/service/**
# Node preload plus its vendored dependency closure (dist/telemetry/node_modules)
!dist/telemetry/**
# webview bundle and stylesheet written by vite build
!dist/webview/**
